{
  "_about": [
    "MATERIALS (Josh, 2026-10-12: 'Material tags for every texture ... Shine where it belongs'). What every texture is, and how it",
    "shines under the helmet lamp and the placed lights (graphics card only; F6 switches it off and on in play, -NoShine / -Shine).",
    "materials: shine = how strong (0 = matte), gloss = how tight the highlight is (higher = smaller, sharper), metal 0..1 = how",
    "much the highlight takes the surface's own colour (gold glints gold), vary = how much the art's own brightness decides it",
    "texel by texel (bright grains and polish shine, painted shadow and cracks do not), wet = how much a wet room's damp shows on it (1 stone .. 0 glass, paintings, characters), relief = its share of the relief (normal) mapping, default 1 (0 on shiny surfaces: Josh, 'relief makes them grainy where they should be shiny'), parallax = its share of the parallax depth (F7 with the relief), default 0: only stone, floor and rock walls and floors (Josh, 2026-10-12: 'limit this to walls and floors, but not the wooden plank style floors').",
    "names: a texture's name (its file name without the number, e.g. 'spacop01') -> material; wins over the rules.",
    "rules: [pattern, material], tried in order on the name, the first that matches wins (patterns are regular expressions).",
    "characterRules: the same for what characters and creatures wear. Otherwise: rooms 'stone', characters 'skin'.",
    "A room's own file can say \"materials\": { \"09-spacop01\": \"copper\", \"or_gold\": { \"shine\": 1.2 } } (by file name or name;",
    "a material, or numbers that override it) and \"shine\": 0.8 (all of that room's shine x 0.8).",
    "Show-Materials.ps1 -Room X lists a room's textures with their material and why."
  ],
